    <div class="qa rv" style="--d: 150ms" id="faq-tabs-template--23927395876979__group_faq_WdDQnK-qa">


      

      <div class="faq-group" data-g="skin-concern" id="faq-tabs-template--23927395876979__group_faq_WdDQnK-group-skin-concern" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="faq-tabs-template--23927395876979__group_faq_WdDQnK-tab-skin-concern">

        

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  Where does this fit in my routine?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">Once you have cleansed your face with a gentle cleanser and patted it dry, take 2-3 drops of the serum and apply evenly on your face. Seal it in with a hydrating moisturizer of your choice. Top it up with SPF 50 in your morning routine. Voilà! That’s your complete routine, simple to stick to.</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  Can I combine Dark Spots &amp; Pore Control Serum with other actives?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">You can, but you probably don’t need to. Dark Spots &amp; Pore Control Serum packs in Niacinamide &amp; Kojic Acid for multi-pathway targeting of melanin production to target pigmentation, while bioretinoids refine the look of the pores for smoother skin texture. Ceramides &amp; peptides in the formula help with barrier repair &amp; structural support, and Stem Cell CM helps the formula’s actives work smarter.<br>
<br>
This serum has been formulated with the effective ingredients your skin needs to get rid of dark spots &amp; reduce visible pore size, so adding several more potent actives to the same routine may simply be more than your skin needs, especially if you’re sensitive or new to active ingredients. Think of it less as needing to add more actives or steps, and more as understanding what’s already doing the work.</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  Bio-retinoids? Do I need to avoid the sun?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">No. Unlike traditional retinol these drive the same renewal morning and night with no sun sensitivity and no irritation. You still want daily SPF, because sun is what creates new pigment, but the serum itself carries no sun restriction.</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  How is this different from a niacinamide or vitamin C serum?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">Those fade what is already on the surface. This one works on the signal that makes the spot in the first place, using sun-safe bio-retinoids and kojic acid, so the pigment is addressed at the source.</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

        

      </div>


      

      <div class="faq-group" data-g="skin-type" id="faq-tabs-template--23927395876979__group_faq_WdDQnK-group-skin-type" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="faq-tabs-template--23927395876979__group_faq_WdDQnK-tab-skin-type" style="display:none;">

        

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  Is it safe for all skin types?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">Yes. It is built on a cica and five-ceramide barrier system to calm while it works. Patch test before first use, and if you are pregnant or breastfeeding, check with your doctor first.</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  Is it suitable for Indian skin?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">The clinical study ran on 36 Indian women aged 24 to 44, so the results on this page were measured on Indian skin rather than borrowed from a trial run somewhere else. The concerns it was built for, perioral pigmentation, sun damage and post-inflammatory marks, are also the ones that show most on Fitzpatrick IV to VI skin.</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  I’m 24. Am I too young to start?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">No. At 24 you are protecting structure rather than trying to repair it later, which is the easier job.<br>
</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  Can I use it during pregnancy?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">Check with your doctor if you are pregnant or breastfeeding. There is no retinol and no salicylic acid in the formula, but that call is your doctor’s to make.</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

        

      </div>


      

      <div class="faq-group" data-g="formula-basics" id="faq-tabs-template--23927395876979__group_faq_WdDQnK-group-formula-basics" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="faq-tabs-template--23927395876979__group_faq_WdDQnK-tab-formula-basics" style="display:none;">

        

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  Which size should I start with?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">10 ml is about 15 days, enough to see how your skin takes it. 30 ml is about 40 days. Two 30 ml bottles is the full 75-day protocol.<br>
</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  Can I use it with my other actives?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">You do not need to. This is the active step. Stacking more retinol or brightening acids on top is what irritates skin and makes pigment worse. Cleanse, this serum, moisturiser, SPF in the morning.</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  What is the conditioned media?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">Growth factors and signalling proteins from adipose-derived stem cells, first used in clinical aesthetics in South Korea. The cells are not in the serum, only the proteins they produce.<br>
</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  Do you use proven actives like niacinamide?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">Yes. Niacinamide is the second ingredient on the list, alongside kojic acid, green tea and the conditioned media.</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  Where is it manufactured?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">In India, in a GMP-certified facility. Actives are sourced from South Korea, France, Belgium, Spain, Germany and the USA.</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

        

      </div>


      

      <div class="faq-group" data-g="shipping" id="faq-tabs-template--23927395876979__group_faq_WdDQnK-group-shipping" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="faq-tabs-template--23927395876979__group_faq_WdDQnK-tab-shipping" style="display:none;">

        

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  When will it arrive?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">Dispatched within 2 to 3 business days. After that, metro deliveries usually take 3 to 5 business days and other regions 5 to 7. Tracking comes by WhatsApp and email when it ships.<br>
</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  What if I miss the delivery?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">The courier tries three times, and you get a WhatsApp message so you can pick a better time. After three attempts the parcel returns to us and reshipping costs ₹100. If it shows as delivered but has not reached you, write to us within 48 hours.<br>
</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  Can I return the serum if it doesn’t work for me?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">Unopened products within 7 days of delivery. Once opened we cannot take it back. If it arrived damaged or wrong, email care@aesthex.in within 48 hours with a photo.<br>
</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  Can I change or cancel my order?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">Not once it is confirmed. The address and the delivery option lock in at that point. Email care@aesthex.in with your order number and we will tell you what is possible.<br>
</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

            
              <details>

                <summary>
                  Why don’t you ever discount?
                </summary>

                <div class="in">
                  <span class="metafield-multi_line_text_field">We do not run sales. The price is the same all year, so there is nothing to wait for.</span>
                </div>

              </details>
            

          

        

